Kubernetes initially worked only with Docker.
Later it introduced container Runtime Interface(CRI) through which any vendor can work as kubernetes container runtime by following (Open Container Initiative)OCI standards.
-->OCI standards
  1. imagespec
  2. Runtimespec


Docker = runC + ContainerD + more features
runC was thr container runtime which was managed by deamon ContainerD.
If we want to run containers alone, we can do it using ContainerD runtime.
-'ctr' is default command line tool which comes with containerD for debugging
-'nerdctl' tool is one of the suggested cmd tools to go with containerD for all operations
-'crictl' is a tool designed by kuberenetes for debugging which goes with all the runtimes which meet oci standards
